Late in the afternoon, I walked down to the river.
The weather was still warm and lovely.
I bought a ticket for a small wooden boat.
The ticket cost seventy kroner.
I went on board and found a good seat on the deck.
The boat sailed very slowly down the river.
There were not many other passengers on the boat.
An older lady sat across from me.
She ate a packed lunch together with her husband.
Her husband smiled happily at her.
We sailed under some big, green trees.
The water was blue and completely still.
I just relaxed and enjoyed the trip.
The sky was still light, even though it was late.
It was a really beautiful Danish spring evening.
I leaned back in the little boat.
I enjoyed the green nature along the river.
It was a perfect end to my day in Odense.
